@* AdminLayout.razor — shell for instructor-facing pages: the drawer
   (AdminSidebar) plus the main column. Desktop: fixed sidebar.
   Mobile (<900px): the sidebar becomes an off-canvas drawer.

   Apply [Authorize(Roles = "Instructor")] on each page using this layout —
   not enforced here, since layouts don't carry auth attributes themselves.

   Do NOT put @rendermode on this layout. A layout receives its page as the
   "Body" RenderFragment parameter, and a render-mode boundary cannot carry a
   RenderFragment — rendering throws "Cannot pass the parameter 'Body' to
   component 'AdminLayout' with rendermode 'InteractiveServerRenderMode'".

   A layout also sits OUTSIDE the render-mode boundary that a routable page's
   own @rendermode creates, so a page-level @rendermode leaves anything
   interactive in here completely inert — the hamburger rendered, looked
   tappable, and silently did nothing. Verified with Playwright at a 390px
   viewport: the page body's "@onclick" worked while the hamburger did not.
   All drawer state therefore lives in AdminSidebar.razor, which declares its
   own @rendermode, mirroring TopNavMenu.razor. *@
@inherits LayoutComponentBase
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<div class="admin-shell">

    <AdminSidebar />

    <div class="main">
        <div class="topbar">
            <div class="breadcrumb">@BreadcrumbLabel</div>
        </div>

        <div class="content">
            @Body
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    // Simple breadcrumb derived from the current path — good enough until
    // there's a reason for something more structured.
    private string BreadcrumbLabel => Nav.Uri.Contains("/admin/lessons/create") ? "Admin / New lesson"
        : Nav.Uri.Contains("/admin/topics/create") ? "Admin / New topic"
        : Nav.Uri.Contains("/admin/sessions/create") ? "Admin / New live session"
        : "Admin / Student progress";
}
